# MeTTa compatibility xfail list
# Format:  <relative-path>  <STATUS>:<CATEGORY>:<id>  [free-form notes]
# STATUS  ∈ COMPILE_FAIL | RUN_EXCEPTION | ASSERT_FAIL
# CATEGORY ∈ FEATURE_PENDING | STDLIB_GAP | SEMANTIC_DIVERGENCE | KNOWN_BUG
#
# A test is EXPECTED_FAIL when its actual STATUS matches the line.
# A mismatch (test fails for a different reason) is reported as REGRESSION.
# A test now passing is reported as UNEXPECTED_PASS — remove its line.
#
# The runner skips files imported by other files in the suite (modules).
# So entries here only need to cover files that run as standalone tests.

# f1_imports COMPILES (f1_moduleC's body resolves, and `import!` works) and fails at run time.
# The higher-order-Bool VerifyError is FIXED; the first assert now dies earlier, on
#   ArrayStoreException: JettaLambda$0
# from `((let $x (get-atoms &self) (get-type $x)))` — a one-element TUPLE whose element is a
# bag-valued application. Quoting it as data stores the lambda object into an Atom[]; it has to
# be LIFTED instead (the multivalued-composition box c1's tail also needs).
#
# Scouted with that assert disabled, f1 then reaches :56 `(match &m (= (f 2) $x) $x)` = `(g 3)`,
# which needs two more things: the match RESULT reduced (`(if (< 2 0) …)` → `(g 3)`), and the
# EXPECTED `(g 3)` left UNREDUCED — codegen resolves it statically to f1_moduleC.g even though
# `g` is not in &self at that point in source order.
f1_imports.metta            RUN_EXCEPTION:KNOWN_BUG:multivalued-tuple-lift        ArrayStoreException on `((let …))`; see notes above
